# Generated render / test artifacts (the test runner recreates tests/out on demand)
tests/out/
out/
*.pdf
# Generated HTML export output (e.g. from docs/examples/html_export.typ)
*.html
# The compiled user manual (docs/manual.pdf) is a build artifact: it is NOT
# tracked (binaries bloat history) and NOT shipped in the package bundle. It is
# published as a GitHub Release asset instead. Build it with
# scripts/build-manual.sh. See RELEASING.md.

# Release bundle output (scripts/build-bundle.sh)
dist/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
.vscode/

# Non-shipped piece sets: kept locally for personal use, NOT redistributed.
# alpha is "free for personal non-commercial use"; california/maestro/staunty are
# CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Only the GPLv2+ sets (cburnett, merida) ship. See LICENSE-PIECES.
src/assets/piece_sets/alpha/
src/assets/piece_sets/california/
src/assets/piece_sets/maestro/
src/assets/piece_sets/staunty/

# Private (local-only): prompts + LLM design discussions, and the agent guide
# (CLAUDE.md plus GOTCHAS.md, the triggered-gotcha overflow it points at).
prompts/
CLAUDE.md
GOTCHAS.md

# Reference screenshots of OTHER chess programs' UIs, kept locally for design
# work (measuring their look pixel-by-pixel). Deliberately never tracked: they
# are third-party product screenshots, nothing in docs/manual.typ references
# docs/assets/img, and attribution is carried by a citation instead. Note this
# is a narrow prefix rule on purpose -- lichess_check_example.jpg in the same
# directory IS tracked, so a blanket ignore would be wrong.
docs/assets/img/[Cc][Bb]_*.png

# Per-developer local helpers (machine-specific / convenience, not shipped).
scripts/install-local.sh

# bench: regeneratable perf artifacts (huge timing traces, scratch PDFs)
bench/out/
